-> the_watching_feeling

=== the_watching_feeling ===

## KEY SCENE: Core anxiety about being observed

PATIENT (hesitant)
"Do you ever feel like... like you're always being [watched]<keyword:gregory.core.being_watched>?"

@pause 0.5

PATIENT
"Not in a paranoid way. I know that sounds paranoid."

PATIENT (nervous)
"It's more like... being [on stage]<keyword:gregory.core.performance>. All the time."

%He swallows visibly, his throat tightening.%<symptom:throat_tension>

PATIENT
"Like everyone is waiting for you to [mess up]<keyword:gregory.core.fear_of_judgment>."

-> childhood_hints

=== childhood_hints ===

## HIGH RAPPORT ONLY: Glimpses of origins

@if rapport >= 70
    NARRATOR
    *Gregory is quiet for a moment. When he speaks again, his voice is softer.*
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "I've been like this for as long as I can remember."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT
    "My parents... they meant well. They just wanted me to be [careful]<keyword:gregory.history.be_careful>."
    
    PATIENT (quiet)
    "'Think before you speak, Gregory.' 'Are you sure about that, Gregory?'"
    
    PATIENT
    "I guess I never stopped [thinking]<keyword:gregory.history.always_anxious>. Before I speak. 
    Before I do anything."
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "I've always been... [careful]<keyword:gregory.pattern.careful>. That's all."
    
    PATIENT
    "There's nothing wrong with being careful."
@endif

-> breakthrough_opportunity

=== breakthrough_opportunity ===

## KEY SCENE: Major contradiction and synthesis opportunity
## TODO: Expand with multiple contradiction paths

NARRATOR
*Gregory unconsciously touches his face, running a hand through his carefully maintained hair.*

## Contradiction: "I take care of myself" vs visual bitten_nails
%His fingernails are bitten down to the quick, the skin around them raw and red.%<symptom:bitten_nails>

PATIENT (dismissive)
"I [take care of myself]<keyword:gregory.coping.self_care_claim>. I have routines."

## If player has caught the contradiction (synthesis successful)
@if synthesis_complete("self_care_claim", "bitten_nails")
    NARRATOR
    *He notices where you're looking. His hand drops quickly to his lap.*
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (caught)
    "I... I didn't even realize I was doing it."
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "The nail thing. It started when I was a kid."
    
    PATIENT
    "I do it when I'm... when things are [too much]<keyword:gregory.emotion.overwhelmed>."
    
    @restore_focus 30
    @set flag breakthrough_self_care
@endif

-> emotional_vulnerability

=== emotional_vulnerability ===

## HIGH RAPPORT PATH: Genuine emotional moments

@if rapport >= 60
    NARRATOR
    *Something shifts in Gregory's expression. The mask slipping, just for a moment.*
    
    PATIENT (exhausted)
    "I'm so [tired]<keyword:gregory.insight.tired_of_pretending>."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT
    "Of pretending everything is fine."
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "Of performing 'okay' for everyone. My boss. My coworkers. My family."
    
    %His eyes glisten slightly, though no tears fall.%<symptom:tear_welling>
    
    PATIENT (quiet)
    "What if they saw what I'm really like? Would they still..."
    
    @pause 0.3
    
    PATIENT
    "Would they still [want me around]<keyword:gregory.core.fear_of_rejection>?"
@else
    PATIENT (controlled)
    "Sorry. I'm rambling again."
    
    PATIENT
    "We don't need to get into all of this."
@endif

-> fear_admission

=== fear_admission ===

## KEY SCENE: The core fear revealed

@if rapport >= 50
    PATIENT (quiet)
    "Can I tell you what I'm really afraid of?"
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT
    "Being seen as [broken]<keyword:gregory.core.fear_broken>."
    
    PATIENT
    "Like there's something fundamentally [wrong]<keyword:gregory.core.something_wrong> with me.
    That everyone else can see but I can't fix."
    
    PATIENT (desperate)
    "What if this is just... [who I am]<keyword:gregory.core.identity_fear>?"
@endif

-> turn_3_conclusion

=== turn_3_conclusion ===

## Rapport-gated conclusions based on breakthrough status

@if flag breakthrough_self_care OR flag breakthrough_sleep OR flag breakthrough_judgment
    NARRATOR
    *Gregory takes a deep breath. Something has shifted - a weight partially lifted.*
    
    PATIENT (relieved)
    "I've never said any of this out loud before."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "Thank you. For not... for not making me feel crazy."
@else
    NARRATOR
    *Gregory's guard remains partially up, though cracks have appeared.*
    
    PATIENT (uncertain)
    "I'm not sure why I'm telling you all this."
    
    PATIENT
    "I hope it's helpful. For whatever you're supposed to figure out about me."
@endif

